# RC-012 — First-Time User Experience

North star: **"I understand this app, and I want to come back."**

## Before changing first-use flows ask

- Does copy explain what ORACLY is AND is not — without mystical jargon?
- Does onboarding reach first reading within one minute?
- Is first reading copy warmer and clearer via `FirstSessionCopy`?
- Are new user defaults honest (zero readings, no fake stats)?
- Did we avoid redesigning Home layout or navigation structure?

If any answer is no — revise.

## Canonical doc

`docs/RC-012.md`

## Out of scope

Home redesign · navigation restructure · premium-before-value

## Success

Calm onboarding. Guided first reading. Obvious next steps.
